From: GloriousEggroll <tcrider84@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Don't send WM_INPUTLANGCHANGE when the layout doesn't change.

A thread's kbd_layout is NULL until its layout is first changed, so the
first ActivateKeyboardLayout() call always looked like a change, even
when the requested layout was the one already in effect. winewayland
requests the current layout on every keyboard focus enter, so every
game got a WM_INPUTLANGCHANGE at startup, which Windows doesn't send.

Enemy Territory: Quake Wars crashes in its WM_INPUTLANGCHANGE handler
when it gets the message during startup, then exits with
"sdUIWindow::ParseKeys: key 'mouse1'".

Compare against the effective layout instead.

Link: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/629
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/win32u/input.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/input.c b/dlls/win32u/input.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -1421,7 +1421,8 @@
     if (!user_driver->pActivateKeyboardLayout( layout, flags ))
         return 0;
 
-    old_layout = info->kbd_layout;
+    /* compare with the effective layout, kbd_layout is NULL until the first change */
+    old_layout = NtUserGetKeyboardLayout( 0 );
     if (old_layout != layout)
     {
         HWND ime_hwnd = get_default_ime_window( 0 );
